WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.526 --> 00:00:03.341
(rocket blast)

00:00:03.341 --> 00:00:04.246
- What's up Believe Nation?

00:00:04.246 --> 00:00:06.481
Today I'm going to talk
about the seven stages

00:00:06.481 --> 00:00:07.720
that each start-up goes through

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.817
to make their first million dollars.

00:00:10.817 --> 00:00:13.484
(hip hop music)

00:00:18.349 --> 00:00:19.916
So I get a lot of entrepreneurs
asking me questions

00:00:19.916 --> 00:00:21.701
about how to make their
first million dollars.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.718
What are the steps that
companies go through?

00:00:23.718 --> 00:00:25.300
What are the stages that
you need to understand

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.970
that most businesses flow through?

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:29.276
And so I thought I'd make this video today

00:00:29.276 --> 00:00:31.468
sharing my thoughts on the seven steps

00:00:31.468 --> 00:00:33.093
that companies go through

00:00:33.093 --> 00:00:36.025
on their process to making
their first million dollars.

00:00:36.025 --> 00:00:38.608
(upbeat music)

00:00:39.464 --> 00:00:41.975
So step number one is you
have to have a dissatisfaction

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.354
with the status quo.

00:00:43.354 --> 00:00:45.530
You have to not like what's
happening around you.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.678
Successful entrepreneurs
have a big dissatisfaction

00:00:47.678 --> 00:00:49.202
with what's currently happening.

00:00:49.202 --> 00:00:50.450
They're not happy with the solutions.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.452
They have a problem,

00:00:51.452 --> 00:00:53.411
either their own problem
or somebody else's problem,

00:00:53.411 --> 00:00:54.557
and they're just not happy

00:00:54.557 --> 00:00:56.165
with the current solutions out there.

00:00:56.165 --> 00:00:59.546
It's the start of every
single great business.

00:00:59.546 --> 00:01:02.898
There has to be a pain
point and a dissatisfaction

00:01:02.898 --> 00:01:05.075
with the current solutions out there.

00:01:05.075 --> 00:01:07.658
(upbeat music)

00:01:08.587 --> 00:01:10.720
Number two is idea generation.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.710
So we have a problem, our own
problem, a friend's problem.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.974
We're dissatisfied with
the solutions out there.

00:01:15.974 --> 00:01:17.686
Now, we got to figure out what's an idea

00:01:17.686 --> 00:01:18.557
that's going to work.

00:01:18.557 --> 00:01:21.692
What's the winning idea that
combines what we love to do,

00:01:21.692 --> 00:01:23.535
what we're super passionate, excited about

00:01:23.535 --> 00:01:26.321
with what's going to solve the problem?

00:01:26.321 --> 00:01:28.440
And there may be multiple
ways to solve this problem.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.153
Whatever problem you're facing right now,

00:01:30.153 --> 00:01:31.749
there could be a million
different ways to solve it,

00:01:31.749 --> 00:01:34.056
but not all of them are
going to work for you,

00:01:34.056 --> 00:01:36.712
and not all of them align with
what you're passionate about.

00:01:36.712 --> 00:01:38.715
And so at the core of
every successful business

00:01:38.715 --> 00:01:41.879
is a combination of
what there's a need for,

00:01:41.879 --> 00:01:43.461
what there's dissatisfaction with,

00:01:43.461 --> 00:01:44.825
what pain point people have

00:01:44.825 --> 00:01:48.003
with what you are super
passionate and excited about,

00:01:48.003 --> 00:01:49.773
and combining those things will lead

00:01:49.773 --> 00:01:52.760
to a successful idea to
launch a business with.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.150
(upbeat music)

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:58.515
Stage number three is, you
actually launch your business.

00:01:58.515 --> 00:02:00.242
And this is where a lot
of people fall down.

00:02:00.242 --> 00:02:03.856
A lot of people get stuck
in just the idea generation,

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:07.354
in the planning, because
it's exciting to plan.

00:02:07.354 --> 00:02:09.197
It's exciting to plan
and see how we can build

00:02:09.197 --> 00:02:11.954
a multi-million empire and
what our life would look like.

00:02:11.954 --> 00:02:13.304
And we get a high from that.

00:02:13.304 --> 00:02:15.248
We get a high from thinking
about what our life

00:02:15.248 --> 00:02:17.500
could look like, but then we
actually have to do the work.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.171
And doing the work kind of
sucks a lot of the time.

00:02:20.171 --> 00:02:21.027
Most of the time.

00:02:21.027 --> 00:02:22.536
And we don't want to do that
work cause we want to stay

00:02:22.536 --> 00:02:24.452
on that high planet where
we're just imagining

00:02:24.452 --> 00:02:26.469
that future vision for ourselves.

00:02:26.469 --> 00:02:28.240
You have to start.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.475
So many people have great, amazing ideas

00:02:30.475 --> 00:02:33.317
and they see other people
make money off of it

00:02:33.317 --> 00:02:34.933
and you claim that that was your idea.

00:02:34.933 --> 00:02:36.747
Well, who cares if it was your idea?

00:02:36.747 --> 00:02:37.580
They had the idea too,

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.562
and they went out and
did something about it.

00:02:39.562 --> 00:02:41.565
And so when you have that great idea,

00:02:41.565 --> 00:02:43.800
you need to actually start.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.333
Where too many people
die with their best ideas

00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:50.449
still in them, you need to
take action on the idea.

00:02:50.449 --> 00:02:53.831
(upbeat music)

00:02:53.831 --> 00:02:56.617
Stage number four is
failure and adjustment.

00:02:56.617 --> 00:03:00.202
A super important thing to
understand is most businesses

00:03:00.202 --> 00:03:02.712
don't end up the way that they planned.

00:03:02.712 --> 00:03:04.120
The thing that actually makes you money,

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.877
that has a big impact,
that helps you explode,

00:03:06.877 --> 00:03:09.664
is very rarely the thing
that you start with.

00:03:09.664 --> 00:03:11.173
So, it's still important to have a plan.

00:03:11.173 --> 00:03:12.494
It's still important to have an idea

00:03:12.494 --> 00:03:13.698
of what you're going to do.

00:03:13.698 --> 00:03:16.688
But recognizing that that
plan is likely going to fail,

00:03:16.688 --> 00:03:18.502
so let's get it out there
as soon as possible.

00:03:18.502 --> 00:03:20.417
And then you need to adjust and tweak

00:03:20.417 --> 00:03:22.885
to what the market wants and
to what you're passionate about

00:03:22.885 --> 00:03:24.481
to build something even better.

00:03:24.481 --> 00:03:25.439
It's super important.

00:03:25.439 --> 00:03:27.500
Most companies, you look
at how they started.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.110
Look at what their first product was

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.837
and look at what they sell now.

00:03:30.837 --> 00:03:32.550
It's totally different.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.930
And they had the willingness
to fail and to adjust.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:39.066
Hewlett-Packard started selling
audio oscillators for films.

00:03:39.066 --> 00:03:41.533
And they sold a couple
audio oscillators for films.

00:03:41.533 --> 00:03:43.202
I don't even know if they
still sell audio oscillators.

00:03:43.202 --> 00:03:44.595
It's not anywhere close to being

00:03:44.595 --> 00:03:46.003
a big part of their business.

00:03:46.003 --> 00:03:47.019
They adjusted.

00:03:47.019 --> 00:03:48.760
Wrigley's started off in the

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:51.837
baking soda or baking powder industry,

00:03:51.837 --> 00:03:54.565
and as a side they happened
to give some gum away.

00:03:54.565 --> 00:03:56.626
So every case that you
bought of their baking soda

00:03:56.626 --> 00:03:59.717
or baking powder, you
would get some gum with it.

00:03:59.717 --> 00:04:01.343
People really liked the gum so he said,

00:04:01.343 --> 00:04:04.216
"Huh, why don't we focus on gum?"

00:04:04.216 --> 00:04:06.161
And then Wrigley's became
this big gum brand.

00:04:06.161 --> 00:04:09.328
And so part of success in any business

00:04:10.355 --> 00:04:12.648
is recognizing that you need
to get through that phase.

00:04:12.648 --> 00:04:14.491
That the great idea that you have,

00:04:14.491 --> 00:04:16.349
no matter how great it looks in your head,

00:04:16.349 --> 00:04:17.829
is not going to be the one that

00:04:17.829 --> 00:04:20.310
ultimately guides you to massive success.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:23.489
It'll be a seed and the
seed will have to grow.

00:04:23.489 --> 00:04:26.043
And it'll grow by testing the
idea, by talking to customers,

00:04:26.043 --> 00:04:28.597
by getting in the market
and then adjusting.

00:04:28.597 --> 00:04:30.963
And too many people make that mistake.

00:04:30.963 --> 00:04:35.142
They launch, it doesn't
work, and then they quit.

00:04:35.142 --> 00:04:37.987
Expect to launch. Expect it not to work.

00:04:37.987 --> 00:04:40.737
And then adjust. Fail and adjust.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.443
That will be your path through.

00:04:43.443 --> 00:04:46.026
(upbeat music)

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:49.321
Phase number five is extending the idea.

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:51.570
This is where a lot of
entrepreneurs also will fall down.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:53.602
They'll have some initial
success with their business.

00:04:53.602 --> 00:04:54.749
And now we're talking about the path

00:04:54.749 --> 00:04:56.406
to being a million-dollar company.

00:04:56.406 --> 00:04:58.394
They'll have some initial
success with their business,

00:04:58.394 --> 00:05:00.440
but they won't expand beyond it.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.994
Where it's very rare that
you could take one product

00:05:02.994 --> 00:05:06.318
in one single market and
build a million-dollar,

00:05:06.318 --> 00:05:07.972
multi-million-dollar company.

00:05:07.972 --> 00:05:10.425
You need to start thinking,
how do I expand this?

00:05:10.425 --> 00:05:12.674
How do I build to more geographic areas?

00:05:12.674 --> 00:05:14.085
How do I expand my product reach?

00:05:14.085 --> 00:05:15.217
How do I add more features?

00:05:15.217 --> 00:05:16.566
How do I create more services?

00:05:16.566 --> 00:05:20.412
How do I add a premium
line or a budget line?

00:05:20.412 --> 00:05:24.115
How do I go beyond my state
or my province or my country?

00:05:24.115 --> 00:05:26.292
How do I build this thing out?

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:28.005
You need to think about
how am I going to extend

00:05:28.005 --> 00:05:28.847
my product line,

00:05:28.847 --> 00:05:30.806
and a lot of it will
come from your customers.

00:05:30.806 --> 00:05:33.258
Again, this is just adjusting
to what the market wants.

00:05:33.258 --> 00:05:35.406
You will find that your
customers will take you places

00:05:35.406 --> 00:05:36.973
that you never even thought of.

00:05:36.973 --> 00:05:39.034
Again, the success in
business comes from combining

00:05:39.034 --> 00:05:41.153
what there's a need for,
what customers want,

00:05:41.153 --> 00:05:43.403
and what you're passionate about creating.

00:05:43.403 --> 00:05:45.376
So as you get out into the
market, one of the best things

00:05:45.376 --> 00:05:48.264
you could do is get as close
to your customers as possible.

00:05:48.264 --> 00:05:50.165
It doesn't make financial
sense if you're selling

00:05:50.165 --> 00:05:52.763
a $20 product to call each customer

00:05:52.763 --> 00:05:54.011
and ask how they're using it.

00:05:54.011 --> 00:05:56.304
But it's so important to do
because it's going to give you

00:05:56.304 --> 00:05:58.118
the feedback on how you can get better.

00:05:58.118 --> 00:05:59.221
How you can improve your product

00:05:59.221 --> 00:06:00.542
to better serve their needs,

00:06:00.542 --> 00:06:02.719
but also how you can extend
it because the more you

00:06:02.719 --> 00:06:05.795
understand their use, the more
you understand their lives,

00:06:05.795 --> 00:06:07.653
the more you understand their business,

00:06:07.653 --> 00:06:10.222
the more you're going to come
up with other creative solutions

00:06:10.222 --> 00:06:11.963
that you can sell into them

00:06:11.963 --> 00:06:13.850
and then you can sell to
a broader market, as well.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:16.070
The way to expand any business,

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:19.103
an easy, fast, simple way to do it

00:06:19.103 --> 00:06:21.832
is to talk to every single customer.

00:06:21.832 --> 00:06:23.225
Understand why they bought it.

00:06:23.225 --> 00:06:25.242
Understand how they're using it.

00:06:25.242 --> 00:06:27.535
And then think about you
can expand your market

00:06:27.535 --> 00:06:30.002
based on what your customers
need or are asking for

00:06:30.002 --> 00:06:31.877
and you have a creative solution for.

00:06:31.877 --> 00:06:35.157
(upbeat music)

00:06:35.157 --> 00:06:37.087
Number six is building a team.

00:06:37.087 --> 00:06:38.219
This is another stumbling block

00:06:38.219 --> 00:06:40.033
that a lot of entrepreneurs fall back on.

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:41.179
So you had some success.

00:06:41.179 --> 00:06:42.253
You built your first product.

00:06:42.253 --> 00:06:43.588
You're getting some results from it.

00:06:43.588 --> 00:06:45.344
You're expanding. You're
building other products.

00:06:45.344 --> 00:06:48.392
At some point there becomes
a huge crutch on your time.

00:06:48.392 --> 00:06:50.467
It's like you can't do more.

00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:51.300
Physically.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.398
You just don't have the time.

00:06:52.398 --> 00:06:53.515
You're maxed out.

00:06:53.515 --> 00:06:55.939
This happens quite early on
for a lot of entrepreneurs.

00:06:55.939 --> 00:06:57.651
You're maxed out, and
so to be able to build

00:06:57.651 --> 00:06:58.986
the multi-million-dollar company

00:06:58.986 --> 00:07:01.178
or getting your first million,
you need to build a team.

00:07:01.178 --> 00:07:02.527
You got to bring people on board.

00:07:02.527 --> 00:07:04.283
You got to bring on people to help you

00:07:04.283 --> 00:07:05.691
get it to the next step.

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:08.243
Even if it starts off part-time.

00:07:08.243 --> 00:07:10.251
My first guy was one hour a day.

00:07:10.251 --> 00:07:12.210
Started off part-time,
moving up, moving up,

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.242
moving up, moving up to
allow you to focus on

00:07:14.242 --> 00:07:16.534
the higher picture
things for your business.

00:07:16.534 --> 00:07:18.711
Here's what happens in a lot of companies.

00:07:18.711 --> 00:07:19.887
You have some success.

00:07:19.887 --> 00:07:21.222
You realize you want to build a team.

00:07:21.222 --> 00:07:23.237
You hire somebody. Great.

00:07:23.237 --> 00:07:25.085
Your first hire doesn't work out.

00:07:25.085 --> 00:07:26.348
Usually the first hire won't work out

00:07:26.348 --> 00:07:29.076
because you suck as a leader.

00:07:29.076 --> 00:07:31.732
You suck as a manager and you
don't know how to hire people.

00:07:31.732 --> 00:07:32.565
And that makes sense.

00:07:32.565 --> 00:07:33.967
If this is the first time you've done it,

00:07:33.967 --> 00:07:35.766
don't expect to bring on a star employee

00:07:35.766 --> 00:07:37.087
the first time through.

00:07:37.087 --> 00:07:38.320
As you work through that process,

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:39.801
you learn how to be a better manager.

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:41.150
You learn how to be a better leader.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:44.474
You learn how to improve your process.

00:07:44.474 --> 00:07:46.984
So that you bring on better
people to start with.

00:07:46.984 --> 00:07:48.247
But what happens to a lot of people

00:07:48.247 --> 00:07:50.822
is they didn't get their first hire right.

00:07:50.822 --> 00:07:52.023
And then they crouch back and say,

00:07:52.023 --> 00:07:54.374
"You know what, I can't
work with other people.

00:07:54.374 --> 00:07:56.420
"I just have to do it all myself."

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:57.828
And you can be really successful.

00:07:57.828 --> 00:07:59.497
Make a couple hundred
thousand dollars a year

00:07:59.497 --> 00:08:01.485
as a solo consultant if
you're one of the best

00:08:01.485 --> 00:08:03.169
at what you do in the world.

00:08:03.169 --> 00:08:04.765
But you don't see a lot of million-dollar

00:08:04.765 --> 00:08:06.681
consultants a year.

00:08:06.681 --> 00:08:10.381
There are a few, but solo
million-dollar consultants a year?

00:08:10.381 --> 00:08:12.892
You don't really see that happen.

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:15.054
Those guys have a team.

00:08:15.054 --> 00:08:16.810
And you need to start to build your team.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.000
If you want to hit a million dollars,

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.656
you need to start building
your team to allow you

00:08:20.656 --> 00:08:22.470
to focus on the higher leverage things.

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:24.618
And expect to make mistakes
with your first team members.

00:08:24.618 --> 00:08:26.577
Expect to hire the wrong people.

00:08:26.577 --> 00:08:28.217
Expect them to make mistakes.

00:08:28.217 --> 00:08:29.784
And expect for you to work on yourself

00:08:29.784 --> 00:08:32.068
to get better as a
leader, manager, recruiter

00:08:32.068 --> 00:08:33.461
so you bring the right people on board.

00:08:33.461 --> 00:08:35.290
'Cause you need to figure out this piece

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:37.148
if you're going to go off
and accomplish big things.

00:08:37.148 --> 00:08:39.731
(upbeat music)

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.430
And number seven is leading the team.

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:44.012
So, we've hired our first person.

00:08:44.012 --> 00:08:45.739
Now we're going to bring on
more people and more people

00:08:45.739 --> 00:08:47.829
and more people and
quickly what you realize

00:08:47.829 --> 00:08:51.588
in a bigger company is
your highest leverage skill

00:08:51.588 --> 00:08:54.679
is going to be getting
the most out of your team

00:08:54.679 --> 00:08:56.159
instead of the productive work that you do

00:08:56.159 --> 00:08:57.262
in your business.

00:08:57.262 --> 00:08:58.945
So, let me explain.

00:08:58.945 --> 00:09:01.674
When you're first starting
off, you're doing everything.

00:09:01.674 --> 00:09:03.691
Your value is 100% of the business.

00:09:03.691 --> 00:09:07.309
When you hire somebody
new to take on a new role,

00:09:07.309 --> 00:09:09.484
you might be both working
the same number of hours,

00:09:09.484 --> 00:09:11.588
but you're maybe adding more
value 'cause you're the CEO.

00:09:11.588 --> 00:09:12.421
You're the founder.

00:09:12.421 --> 00:09:14.984
But let's say it's like
40% them and 60% you.

00:09:14.984 --> 00:09:17.074
Or 70% you, 30% them.

00:09:17.074 --> 00:09:17.907
Great.

00:09:17.907 --> 00:09:19.019
As you add more people, though,

00:09:19.019 --> 00:09:20.586
your percentage keeps coming down.

00:09:20.586 --> 00:09:22.952
You may be the single most
important person in the business

00:09:22.952 --> 00:09:27.625
but collectively your team is
doing way more than you are.

00:09:27.625 --> 00:09:29.642
If I look at this business
with this YouTube channel

00:09:29.642 --> 00:09:31.601
we've got eight people
working on making this channel

00:09:31.601 --> 00:09:33.981
happen for you guys every single day.

00:09:33.981 --> 00:09:36.826
I contribute the most value.

00:09:36.826 --> 00:09:38.596
Sorry, guys on my team.

00:09:38.596 --> 00:09:41.731
But I don't do, like collectively,
my team does way more

00:09:41.731 --> 00:09:44.982
than I do 'cause I can't
do all this stuff myself.

00:09:44.982 --> 00:09:47.695
And so understanding
that you need to not just

00:09:47.695 --> 00:09:50.163
focus on what you are
contributing to the business,

00:09:50.163 --> 00:09:51.977
your day-to-day tasks and activities,

00:09:51.977 --> 00:09:55.742
but your most important
activity is building up

00:09:55.742 --> 00:09:57.538
the people on your team.

00:09:57.538 --> 00:10:00.121
'Cause if they get better,
your company gets way,

00:10:00.121 --> 00:10:01.688
way, way better.

00:10:01.688 --> 00:10:03.996
As you continue to build your team,

00:10:03.996 --> 00:10:06.768
your value, in terms of
the tasks you provide,

00:10:06.768 --> 00:10:09.293
become decreasingly and
decreasingly important,

00:10:09.293 --> 00:10:11.920
because your team takes over
much more of the enterprise.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.517
And so shifting your priorities
to focusing on your team

00:10:14.517 --> 00:10:15.635
and building them up

00:10:15.635 --> 00:10:17.318
will have a much bigger
impact to help you get to

00:10:17.318 --> 00:10:19.672
not just a million dollars,
but way through it, too.

00:10:19.672 --> 00:10:21.602
So those are my thoughts
on the seven stages

00:10:21.602 --> 00:10:23.779
that start-ups go through
to make their first million.

00:10:23.779 --> 00:10:25.651
I'd love to know, what do you guys think?

00:10:25.651 --> 00:10:28.124
What point resonated most with you?

00:10:28.124 --> 00:10:29.360
What do you need to work on the most

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:30.884
to help you break that barrier?

00:10:30.884 --> 00:10:32.857
And am I missing an eight,
nine, ten that you guys

00:10:32.857 --> 00:10:34.236
want to add to the list?

00:10:34.236 --> 00:10:35.069
Share some love.

00:10:35.069 --> 00:10:36.500
I'd love to hear from
you down in the comments

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:39.127
and help the fellow
people of Believe Nation.

00:10:39.127 --> 00:10:40.709
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:10:40.709 --> 00:10:41.623
I believe in you.

00:10:41.623 --> 00:10:43.568
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:10:43.568 --> 00:10:45.788
and whatever your one word is.

00:10:45.788 --> 00:10:46.659
Much love.

00:10:46.659 --> 00:10:48.159
I'll see you soon.

